  "content": {
    "title": "Final Four scores, results: Michigan throttles Arizona in one-sided beatdown, UConn tops Illinois to set up NCAA tournament title game",
    "text": "UConn and Michigan will square off in the national championship game on Monday night at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis, which will officially wrap up the 2025-26 college basketball season.UConn set to play for 3rd title in 4 yearsIllinois entered the Final Four with the best offense in college basketball. It wasn’t enough on Saturday to overcome UConn’s disciplined defense and inside-out attack.AdvertisementUConn disrupted Illinois’ normally efficient offense and rode its own balanced attack to a 71-62 win in Saturday’s first national semifinal. When Illinois threatened to rally from a 13-point second-half deficit, it looked to a familiar face.Braylon Mullins, the hero of UConn’s Elite Eight thriller over Duke, hit a late 3 to help ice the win after a previously scoreless second half.With the win, UConn advances to Monday’s national championship game, where it will seek its third NCAA title in four seasons. It will face the winner of Saturday’s second Final Four game between Arizona and Michigan.Read more about UConn’s gritty win here. AdvertisementMichigan routs Arizona in one-sided affairMichigan didn’t take much time to make it clear it is the favorite to win the national championship.The Wolverines blitzed Arizona in the first half on the way to a 91-73 Final Four win. Michigan will play UConn on Monday night in the national title game. And it was the fifth time in five games during the 2026 NCAA tournament that Michigan scored at least 90 points.Michigan led by 16 at halftime as the Wildcats faced their largest deficit of the season just halfway into the first half when the Wolverines were up 26-10. And it was far from a perfect half for Michigan too. That’s how much Michigan outplayed Arizona.AdvertisementRead more about Michigan’s blowout of Arizona here.See how it all played out below:FINAL — No. 2 UConn 71, No. 3 Illinois 62FINAL — No. 1 Michigan 91, No. 1 Arizona 73Live coverage is over65 updatesSat, April 4, 2026 at 7:38 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffSat, April 4, 2026 at 10:57 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffArizona made its first Final Four since 2001 and won a school-record 36 games this season, but it all came to a crashing end on Saturday with a blowout loss to Michigan.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:50 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Michigan star said he plans to play in Monday’s title game despite hurting his ankle.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:42 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffSat, April 4, 2026 at 10:35 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Wolverines are scoring a ton and winning by a ton in every game so far this tournament. Can they keep it going for one more?Michigan is the only team to ever score 90 or more points AND win by double digits in five consecutive games in the same NCAA Tournament, per CBS Sports research.Goliath.— Matt Norlander (@MattNorlander) April 5, 2026Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:33 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Wolverines dominate wire-to-wire and advance to the national championship, where it will face UConn on Monday night.Michigan is going for its first men’s basketball title since 1989.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:23 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Wolverines lead 88-66 at the final media timeout. They’re 3:02 away from advancing to the national championship.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:11 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffArizona is finally knocking down a few shots but this game is still comfortably in the Wolverines’ hands. Michigan leads 81-60 with 7:33 to go.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 10:03 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffYaxel Lendeborg has played 7 minutes so far in the second half but is nursing his ankle on the sideline when he checks out.At this point, the biggest question may be his status for the title game.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:58 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Wolverines have made their last 7 shots and are 9 of 13 in the second half. That’s how they’ve built a massive 72-45 lead with 12:17 to play.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:48 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffAll Yaxel Lendeborg did was come back in on a tender ankle and drill two straight 3-pointers to open the half. Michigan leads 56-39.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:40 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffWe’re back in action for the final half of this Final Four matchup. Good news for Michigan as Yaxel Lendeborg is back in the game after playing just 5 minutes in the first half due to an ankle injury.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:32 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffMichigan’s veteran roster is overwhelming the younger Wildcats, who have turned it over 9 times and have just 2 assists so far. No Arizona player has more than 6 points.Michigan 48, Arizona 32 at half despite all kinds of foul trouble and getting only a few minutes from Lendeborg. Experience delta showing up. Arizona just skittish from the jump.— Dan Wolken (@DanWolken) April 5, 2026Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:18 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffAday Mara has 15 points to lead Michigan and the Wolverines are pretty much doing everything better than the Wildcats so far.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:10 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffMichigan responded to Arizona’s scoring burst with one of its own. The scoring his coming from up and down the lineup as seven different Wolverines players have at least 5 points. Michigan leads 38-25 late in the 1st.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:08 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffLendeborg hasn’t returned to the game since hurting his ankle and now he’s back in the locker room to receive icing and treatment, per the broadcast.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 9:01 PM CDTNick BrombergArizona needs to strike now — and try to get a third foul on any of Michigan’s three frontcourt starters.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 8:53 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe Wildcats are finally coming to life as an 11-2 run has cut Michigan’s lead to 28-21 at the under-8 timeout.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 8:50 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffThe star Michigan big man appeared to tweak his ankle while driving to the basket. He’s in some pain and walked to the locker room with a limp after staying in to shoot free throws.Sat, April 4, 2026 at 8:41 PM CDTYahoo Sports StaffMichigan is dominating so far and it has the Wildcats in their biggest deficit of the season, trailing 22-10.Can Arizona do something it really hasn’t had to all season and rally?Sat, April 4, 2026 at 8:34 PM CDTNick BrombergThe Wolverines’ star picked up two fouls in five seconds and left the game with 18:38 to go. Yet Michigan has not struggled in his absence.How long will he sit?",
